ived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-03-22T01:08:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T05:22:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.4 stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot 4.4 2D scene zoom buttons zoom differently than Godot 4.3\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen a new project and toggle 2D. In the top left press the plus/minus buttons.\n\nPressing the plus/minus buttons in the top left of the 2D scene window was not perfect but in 4.3 you were able to zoom to some convenient zoom levels. Like: 25%, 50%, 200%, 400%, 800%, 1600%, etc. This is no longer the case in 4.4.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c083a84a-c6c6-48db-877a-4f224d64bd7b)\n\nThe only way to get to these zoom levels is to use the keyboard by pressing 1-5 keys (or shift 1-5), however it imprecisely centers' on your cursor position. So you have to constantly press F to center onto your selection.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo need, just create a new project.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104464/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104464/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null}